{
  "format": "rg.ui_roles/1",
  "source": "The design language's role contract (docs/design_language.md). Every UI colour of both games is one of these roles; a palette gives each a colour. contrast_classes: 'text' 4.5 and 'large_text' 3.0 and 'graphic' 3.0 [C WCAG 2.2 SC 1.4.3 / 1.4.11]; 'quiet' 1.5 [AS] for marks that repeat a reading and carry no information of their own (minor ticks, off lamps, grid lines). fixed colours are the worst cases behind a translucent surface: a sunlit field, a bright sky and a night scene [AS], read off nothing. sits_on: a surface that is always drawn on another one, so what is behind it is that surface and not the scene. lightness_distinct 18 L* [AS] keeps the signals that carry no word apart without hue: lamps, pedal bars, the redline. A badge or a status line says what it means in words. simulated_vision matrices: Machado, Oliveira, Fernandes 2009, severity 1.0 [C, transcribed from memory, no download], applied in linear sRGB. simulated_distinct 14 Delta E76 [AS].",
  "contrast_classes": { "text": 4.5, "large_text": 3.0, "graphic": 3.0, "quiet": 1.5 },
  "fixed": {
    "bright_field": "#d8dc8f",
    "bright_sky": "#eaf2fa",
    "night": "#04060a",
    "widget_glyph": "#ffffff"
  },
  "default_over": ["bright_field", "bright_sky", "night"],
  "sits_on": {
    "surface_control": "surface_panel",
    "surface_control_hover": "surface_panel",
    "surface_control_pressed": "surface_panel",
    "surface_control_disabled": "surface_panel",
    "surface_note": "surface_panel",
